// EXPECT: E0204 — 300 does not fit `u8`, even inside a `cast`
//
// ADR-0037 §2: a `cast` supplies a *context*, and ADR-0016 §1 already says an
// integer literal takes its type from its context and must fit it. So this is the
// same error `x: u8 = 300;` raises, reusing the same code — the cast's fit check
// is not a second implementation.
main :: () {
    n := cast(u8, 300);
}
